  "limitations": [
    "The Mezo runtime in this evidence remains historical. Current execution identity resolves through accepted Contracts resource contract-bridge-v13-probes-2026-08-24, which proves wrapper-v6/execution-generation-6 behavior after block 11358000.",
    "web3_clientVersion identifies the queried RPC node's software and is not block-pinned consensus evidence for every validator. The fixed-block precompile code/state and source-defined interface are recorded separately.",
    "The ten deployed ERC-20 mappings are point-in-time discovery evidence, not ten supported MDK routes; only the two representative directions above received end-to-end completion proof.",
    "The sampled Ethereum transfers used implementation 0x7e99...6cd9. The post-upgrade implementation and configuration are separately pinned at block 25781632; historical calldata success is not evidence that a current write will succeed.",
    "The official explorer's proxy history supplies all five activations. Exact Match and independently reproduced bytecode apply to the current implementation through the canonical Contract record; no source-verification label is inferred for the first three historical implementations.",
    "A successful, logless Mezo bridge system transaction and an advanced sequence do not alone prove ERC-20 delivery because version-matched keeper source can skip a blocked recipient, missing mapping, or failed ERC-20 mint. Post-state or equivalent recipient delivery evidence is required.",
    "Outflow limits, capacities, reset height, pause authority, minimum amounts, fees, bridge sequence, owner, and validator state are volatile snapshots and must be read again before any future writer.",
    "No timing SLA is inferred from the 930-second and 336-second sample delivery intervals."
  ]
